  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri. M.P Aravinda vs State Of Karnataka on 25 March, 2024 Author: K.Natarajan Bench: K.Natarajan -1- Nc: 2024:Khc:12318 Crl.P No. 3823 of 2022 In The High Court Of Karnataka At Bengaluru Dated This The 25Th Day Of March, 2024 Before The Hon'Ble Mr Justice K.Natarajan Criminal Petition No. 3823 Of 2022 Between: 1. Sri. M.P. Aravinda, S/O Late M. Parameshwarappa, Aged About 48 Years, Agriculturist, R/At Mongote Village, Synsyasikodamaggai Post, Holehonnur Hobli, Bhadravathi Tq, Shivamogga Dist - 577 243. 2. Dr. M.P. Mallikarjuna, S/O Late M. Parameshwarappa Aged About 45 Years, Designated Officer Bbmp Area Digitally North Zone, Office/O Food signed by V Krishna Safety And Standard Of India, Location: Bbmp Area North Zone, High Court of Public Health Zone, Karnataka Sheshadri Road, Bangalore - 560 001. Also At Dr M.P Mallikarjuna, S/o Late M. Parameshwarappa Aged About 43 Years Residing At No.D/4/10, Platinum City Apartment, -2- Sri. M.P Aravinda vs State Of Karnataka on 25 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/82199702/ 1 Nc: 2024:Khc:12318 Crl.P No. 3823 of 2022 Hmt Factory Main Road, Peenya Bangalore - 560 022. ...Petitioners (By Sri. Srinivas N., Advocate) And: 1. State Of Karnataka By Holehonnur Police Station, Bhadaravathi - 577 301, Rep. By Spp High Court Of Karnataka Bangalore - 560 001. 2. Sri. M. Chandrappan S/O Late Mudigowdra Channappa, Aged About 73 Years, Agriculturist, R/O Mongote Village, Synyasikodamaggi Post, Holehonnur Hobli, Bhadravathi Tq, Shivamogga Dist - 577 243. ...Respondents (By Smt. Anitha Girish, Hcgp For R1; Sri. Rudrappa P., Advocate For R2) This Crl.P Is Filed U/S.482 Of Cr.P.C Praying To Quash The Proceedings Pending Against Them In Cr.No.212/2021 For The Offence P/U/S 181, 182, 418, 420, 465, 468, 471, 474, 504, 506 R/W 34 Of Ipc By The Holehonnur Police Station, Which Now Is Pending On The File Of I Additional Civil Judge And J.M.F.C., -3- Nc: 2024:Khc:12318 Crl.P No. 3823 of 2022 Bhadravathi, Be [LEAKAGE_MASK] So Far As It Relates To The Petitioner Is Concerned. This Petition, Coming On For Admission, This Day, The Court Made The Following: Sri. M.P Aravinda vs State Of Karnataka on 25 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/82199702/ 2 Order",
    "facts": "Hence, he has filed the private complaint before the Magistrate under Section 200 of Cr.P.C., which is under challenge. Respondent No.2 also filed a suit for partition which is pending before the Civil Court.",
    "arguments": "He did not file the complaint before the police, and subsequently, if the complaint is not NC: 2024:KHC:12318 registered, he may approach the Superintendent of police under Section 154(3) of Cr.P.C. Therefore, he approached the Magistrate and the Magistrate has referred the complaint to the police for registering the FIR. Whereas the other family members are left out in the partition. Hence, he prays for dismissal of the petition."
  },
